{{DISPLAYTITLE: <span style="color: #b300b3;">Skeleton Army</span>}}
{{Protection}}{{MagicWords}}{{ClashofClansLink}}

{{Card Infobox|Cost=3|Rarity=Epic|Type=Troop|Arena=P.E.K.K.A.'s Playhouse|ReleaseDate=4 January 2016}}{{SubpageNavBox|Evolution=yes}}{{Quote|Spawns an army of Skeletons. Meet Larry and his friends Harry, Gerry, Terry, Mary, etc.}}

The Skeleton Army is an {{Rarity|Epic}} [[Cards|card]] that is unlocked from [[Arenas|P.E.K.K.A's Playhouse (Arena 6)]]. It spawns 15 [[Skeletons]] in a scatter formation. A Skeleton Army card costs 3 [[Elixir]] to deploy.

==Strategy==
{{Battle Deck with Card|:Category:Battle Decks using the Skeleton Army Card}}
*Due to their high numbers and overall very high DPS, the Skeleton Army is very effective against single target enemy [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] and [[:Category:Building Cards|building]]-targeting troops such as the [[P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Mighty Miner]], [[Prince]], [[Lumberjack]], [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Elite Barbarians]], [[Knight]], [[Golden Knight]], [[Hog Rider]], [[Miner]], [[Goblin Giant]], [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Ram Rider]], [[Battle Ram]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Boss Bandit]], [[Monk]], [[Elixir Golem]], [[Rune Giant]], [[Royal Giant]], or the [[Giant]].
**Another benefit is the Skeleton Army's low cost of 3 [[Elixir]], making it a very versatile [[Cards|card]] that can give the player an Elixir advantage in almost any case.
**Although they have low health individually, their sheer numbers allow for them to be effective at blocking most troops and siege buildings. This can even work for air troops, such as the [[Inferno Dragon]] due to the fact that the Skeleton Army can stall and pull the Inferno Dragon away from the tower, giving the [[Tower Princess]] a chance to destroy the Inferno Dragon. The same also applies to the [[Phoenix]], [[Electro Dragon]], [[Flying Machine]], and the [[Mega Minion]].
*While being powerful in numbers, they are very weak against splash damage and [[:Category:Spell Cards|spells]]; most area damage units will be able to take out the whole swarm without losing health, while low cost spells will take out the swarm quickly and efficiently.
**Despite their area damage weakness, the Skeleton Army is capable of countering directional area damage troops like a [[Wizard]], [[Witch]], [[Princess]], [[Ice Wizard]], or [[Bomber]]. For this to work, the Skeleton Army must be placed directly on top of the unit, surrounding it and overwhelming their area damage before the swarm is defeated. The player must also have the assistance of a [[:Category:Crown Towers|Crown Tower]] to damage down the troop, as otherwise there is a chance the Skeletons could clump up in such a way that the troop could eliminate them all before being defeated.
**The Skeleton Army can bait the opponent into using their area damage spell, allowing the player to use other high DPS swarms such as [[Goblin Gang]] safely. However, unlike the Goblin Gang, the Skeleton Army can be fully countered by a wider range of spells. As such, they may not the most effective at baiting out the desired spell, such as [[The Log]], if they have more than one.
**Other swarm troops such as [[Barbarians]], [[Royal Recruits]], and [[Minion Horde]] may be more favorable as a substitute, as they have higher hitpoints compared to the Skeleton Army. However, they also have a heavier Elixir cost, which does make them more committal but also makes them more enticing for the opponent to use a higher cost spell like [[Fireball]] on them, allowing other spell-vulnerable cards in the player's [[Battle Decks|deck]] to thrive.
**[[Poison]] and Fireball are a negative Elixir trade but do counter the Skeleton Army effectively. However, it is still desirable if the spells can hit other troops too as well.
**The [[Barbarian Barrel]] can not only counter the Skeleton Army for a positive Elixir trade but might also force out a response from the opponent. If the Barbarian Barrel is played right at the river, the Barbarian that spawns will get one hit on the Tower Princess left unattended, allowing for minor chip damage. The [[Royal Delivery]] can be utilized in a similar way.
*The Skeleton Army's high troop count may cause some Skeletons to be out of range of their target, missing a lot of would-be damage from the target. Because of this, they do not pair very well with other melee troops, as they will occupy more space, decreasing the number of Skeletons that are attacking even further. However, this limitation will not appear with allied ranged troops.
*The [[Witch]] works well with the Skeleton Army because she can help spawn more [[Skeletons]] to help out. However, be careful doing this as it may cause the opponent to use spells to kill all the Skeletons and possibly defeat the Witch and cause an Elixir loss.
*The Skeleton Army is not recommended to be used offensively, as they can be easily wiped out with spells such as [[Arrows]]. However, if the opponent's cheap spell is out of rotation, this play may force non-efficient counters out of their hand, as if the Skeleton Army manages to lock on to a Crown Tower, they will deal extremely high damage to or even destroy it.
*Cheap ranged swarms like the [[Archers]] and [[Spear Goblins]] are great counters to an offensive Skeleton Army. Their range allows them to kill each Skeleton from a safe distance. Along with the Tower Princess, they can defeat the Skeleton Army while allowing for a slight counterattack afterwards.
*The Skeleton Army cannot target air troops. As such, cheap air swarms like [[Minions]] and [[Bats]] make great counters to it. Similarly, air splash cards like the [[Baby Dragon]] and [[Skeleton Dragons]] can also counter them.
*Their high count allows them to be played in the center or behind the player's [[King's Tower]] to cover both lanes. This often entirely deters the opponent from immediately attacking, as they will only be able to spell down half of the swarm with one push.
*If the player has no spells, then the Skeleton Army will be able to negate the damage from a [[Goblin Barrel]]. When played behind the Crown Tower, it will cover all positions except the front tiles.
*When defending against the [[Goblin Drill]], the player should wait until the Goblin Drill appears on the surface and then deploy the Skeleton Army to counter it, otherwise the Goblin Drill's spawn damage would OHKO most of the Skeletons. The same tactic should also be used when using it to defend against the Skeletons spawned from a [[Skeleton Barrel]].
*If the player has no other cards to effectively counter an [[Electro Giant]], the Skeleton Army will deal some limited damage to him. Keep in mind that they will likely all die, but the Electro Giant will be weakened.
*Using a [[Rage]] on the Skeleton Army makes it a huge threat since they already move quite fast and deal high damage per second. [[Mirror]]ing or [[Clone|Cloning]] the Skeleton Army gives a huge numbers advantage. However, trying either of these strategies is very risky, as a splash unit or a spell can wipe it out for a positive Elixir trade. Additionally, the [[Goblin Curse]] may be a serious threat as it produces 60 goblins for 2 elixir.
*Defensively, [[Freeze]] + Skeleton Army is capable of destroying many ground based troops that would otherwise obliterate it, like [[Valkyrie]], [[Mega Knight]], [[Dark Prince]], and Electro Giant. However, it is very volatile, as the Skeleton Army is frail and vulnerable to spells.
*An [[Ice Golem]] is able to eliminate the entire Skeleton Army with his death damage when equally leveled for a positive Elixir trade.
*If a friendly [[Skeleton King]] is alive, the player can try to accumulate the Skeleton King's ability by placing down the Skeleton Army and expecting the opponent to defeat it. The Skeleton Army is enough to fully accumulate the Skeleton King's ability, allowing for a threatening push.
**On the other hand, the player should not place the Skeleton Army if an enemy Skeleton King is alive, as it could allow him to create a devastating push through this tactic.

