==Trivia== 
*The word "''Skeleton''" comes from the Greek "''σκελετός''" (''skeletós''), meaning dried up or withered.
**The Skeleton Army is 1 of 15 [[cards]] associated with [[Skeletons]], with the others being [[Bomber]], [[Skeleton Dragons]], [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Tombstone]], [[Bomb Tower]], [[Guards]], [[Witch]], [[Balloon]], [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Super Witch]], [[Graveyard]], [[Skeleton King]], and of course, Skeletons.
***In the French and Russian language settings of the game, the Skeleton Army's name translates to "Army of Skeletons". In the Italian and Japanese language settings of the game, the Skeleton Army's name translates to "Skeleton Horde" and "Skeleton Troops" respectively.
***Before 2/9/2021, the Skeleton Army's card render was similar to the Skeletons' card render, only having one additional Skeleton.
*The Skeleton Army is one of the first [[:Category:Troop Cards|troop]] cards to be featured in a [[Training Camp|Trainer]]'s [[Battle Decks|deck]], alongside the [[Minions]], [[Archers]], [[Knight]], [[Spear Goblins]], [[Goblins]], Bomber, Skeletons, [[Barbarians]], [[Minion Horde]], [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Mini P.E.K.K.A]], [[Musketeer]], [[Giant]], [[Valkyrie]], [[Wizard]], [[Hog Rider]], [[Baby Dragon]], Witch, [[P.E.K.K.A.|P.E.K.K.A]], [[Prince]], and Balloon.
*The Skeleton Army is one of the first troop cards to receive a card render, alongside the Archers, Knight, Goblins, Bomber, Skeletons, Barbarians, [[Bats]], [[Royal Recruits]], Skeleton Barrel, [[Rascals]], Musketeer, Giant, Valkyrie, Wizard, [[Flying Machine]], Hog Rider, [[Royal Hogs]], [[Dart Goblin]], [[Zappies]], [[Elixir Golem]], Baby Dragon, Witch, P.E.K.K.A, Prince, Balloon, Giant Skeleton, [[Goblin Giant]], [[Hunter]], [[Electro Dragon]], Wall Breakers, [[Bowler]], [[Cannon Cart]], [[Mega Knight]], [[Ram Rider]], [[Miner]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Ice Wizard]], [[Magic Archer]], [[Bandit]], [[Lava Hound]], [[Night Witch]], and [[Fisherman]].
*The Skeleton Army is 1 of 23 cards that has had its [[Elixir]] cost changed, the others being Bomber, [[Fire Spirit]], Royal Recruits, [[Cannon]], [[Mortar]], Musketeer, [[Three Musketeers]], [[Heal]], [[Goblin Hut]], Bomb Tower, [[Barbarian Hut]], [[Furnace]], [[Elixir Collector]], P.E.K.K.A., Wall Breakers, [[Electro Giant]], Bowler, [[Goblin Barrel]], [[Barbarian Barrel]], [[Rage]], Fisherman, and the [[Monk]].
*According to the [[Version History#Balance Changes (1/10/2018)|1/10/2018 balance changes]], the names of the Skeletons are "Larry", "Harry", "Gerry", "Terry", "Mary", "Barry", "Cherry", "Karrie", "Faerie", "Scary", "Sherry", "Gary", "McClary", "Huckleberry", and "Doot"/"Ledoot".
**The Skeleton "Larry" in the Skeleton Army's description is a reference to the Clash of Clans [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=434cGQAc3E0 Larry commercial].
**In the French language setting of the game, 5 of the Skeletons' names are "Kévin", "Kenny", "Katie", "Karim", and "Kelly". In the Spanish language setting of the game, 4 of the Skeletons' names are "Adolfo", "Astolfo", "Rodolfo", and "Ataúlfo". In the Italian language setting of the game, 5 of the Skeletons' names are "Gino", "Pino", "Dino", "Lino", and "Rino". In the Dutch language setting of the game, 5 of the Skeletons' names are "Harry", "Barry", "Eddy", "Tommy", and "Mary". In the Norwegian language setting of the game, 5 of the Skeletons' names are "Inge", "Ingar", "Ingvart", "Ingve", and "Inghild". In the Portuguese language setting of the game, 5 of the Skeletons' names are "Tico", "Teco", "Taco", "Toco", and "Tuco". In the Finnish language setting of the game, 5 of the Skeletons' names are "Lari", "Jari", "Kari", "Sari", and "Mari".
**According to the [[Version History#Tournaments Update (4/7/2016)|Tournaments Update]], the Skeleton that was removed from the [[Version History#Balance%20Changes%20(21/6/2016)|21/6/2016 balance changes]] joined the Skeleton Army. However, it was removed from the Skeleton Army in the [[Version History#Balance Changes (20/10/2016)|20/10/2016 balance changes]], but it returned back in the 1/10/2018 balance changes.
***The Skeleton's name was "Ledoot", which was a reference to the [https://knowyourmeme.com/memes/skull-trumpet-doot-doot Skull Trumpet] meme.
*The Skeleton Army spawns the most troops of all troop cards, with a total of 15 Skeletons.
*Along with the Skeletons and [[Wizard Trio]], the Skeleton Army is the only swarm card whose members spawn all at the exact same time.
*Even though the Skeleton Army spawns 15 Skeletons, the card render displays 6 Skeletons.
*In the card image, each Skeleton appears to have a diagonal cross on its eye.
*The Skeleton Army is 1 of 2 "value pack" troop card that has a different rarity with its corresponding "basic" troop card, the other being Wizard Trio (the Skeletons are a {{Rarity|Common}} card while the Skeleton Army is an {{Rarity|Epic}} card).
*Using the Skeletons card to summon 15 Skeletons would cost 5 Elixir, whereas using the Skeleton Army card to summon 15 Skeletons costs 3 Elixir.
*The Skeleton Army was featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kIGdeKaT_is The Crown Duel Tournament], by a player called Backstabx.
*Before the Skeletons Army' card release, the Skeletons' hitpoints and damage were increased by 8%.

